        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Templemichael Glebe, Longford town, a long established and most sought-after residential development. No.47 is a bungalow style property, well placed along the inner circle of homes.\r\n\r\nAccommodation Includes  :\r\nEntrance Hall  :  4.0 x 1.9 + 6.2 x 0.9. Laminate flooring.\r\nLiving room  :  4.3 x 4.6.  Laminate flooring, Open fireplace, display unit.\r\nKitchen / Dining area  :  7.3 x 3.3.  Solid fuel stove, fitted units, tiled floor.\r\nSun-room  :  3.0 x 2.2.\r\nBedroom 1.  :  3.6 x 3.1.. Laminate flooring, wardrobe.\r\nBedroom2.  :  3.6 x 2.4.  Wardrobe.\r\nBedroom 3.  :  3.3 x 2.4. Laminate flooring.\r\nBedroom 4.  :  2.9 x 3.2 Laminate flooring, wardrobe.\r\nBathroom  :  3.2 x 1.6  (inc. hot press) Wall & floor tiling.\r\n\r\n\r\nOut-offices  : \r\nGarage  :  2.8 x 5.7.\r\nGarden shed  : 5.1 x 2.2.\r\n\r\nServices  : Mains water and sewerage.\r\nTo the front there is a lawn area, boundary wall and vehicular entrance, lawn, and mature planting to sides and rear.\r\n\r\nThis property will require considerable renovation and up-grades. It has been vacant for more than two years. It may qualify for generous funding under the Vacant Property Refurbishment scheme.\r\nThis scheme provides up to €50,000-00 to renovate a vacant property and up to €70,000 for a derelict property. The fund (Croí Cónaithe) is designed to bring empty buildings back into use as permanent homes or rental properties."
      },
